instruction:
Please set up a VS Code user keybinding so that pressing ctrl+j moves focus from the integrated terminal to the active editor. Add this exact entry to my user keybindings file at /home/user/.config/Code/User/keybindings.json (the file should be a valid JSON array and include this object):

{ "key": "ctrl+j", "command": "workbench.action.focusActiveEditorGroup", "when": "terminalFocus" }

It’s fine if this overrides a conflicting default. Reference: https://superuser.com/questions/1270103/how-to-switch-the-cursor-between-terminal-and-code-in-vscode
